    29	#     - both prototype families appear; exactly one sprite has scale 2 or 3
    30	#     - sprites are separated, so connected-component extraction still isolates them cleanly
    31	#   output_view:
    32	#     - the original scattered layout disappears entirely
    33	#     - swapped sprites are re-drawn in a common left-side strip
    34	#     - they are stacked vertically with a 1-cell gap between consecutive sprites
    35	#   local_trace_example:
    36	#     - original task: a scale-3 proto_A instance at bottom-right is replaced by scale-3 proto_B
    37	#       and kept anchor-aligned near bottom-right
    38	#     - new task: the same instance is still identified as proto_A at scale 3, but after swapping
    39	#       it is pasted into the next slot of the shared stack strip instead of its old location
    40	#     - difference: identification logic is unchanged; only destination layout changes
    41	#
    42	# b) complexity_calibration:
    43	#   - keeping two nontrivial prototypes plus multiple scales preserves the original matching burden
    44	#   - stacking all outputs into one strip makes the D5 change visually strong
    45	#   - ordering uses visible geometry only (reading order of input bboxes), not color ids
    46	#   - using a vertical stack avoids accidental simplification where outputs still resemble the
    47	#     original dispersed layout
    48	#
    49	# c) implicit_assumption_review_for_original_main:
    50	#   - extracting connected components still works because sprites remain non-overlapping
    51	#   - "smallest-area sprites reveal the two prototypes" must still hold, so the generator keeps
    52	#     one scale-1 instance of each prototype
    53	#   - scale inference still assumes the anchor region scales by the same integer factor
    54	#   - the old code's in-place clearing and anchor-based re-placement depended on destination
    55	#     staying local; this is the exact assumption removed here
    56	#   - the new output cannot start from a copy of the input, otherwise stale original sprites would
    57	#     remain; it must start from an all-background canvas
    58	#
